 . .","note":"now in a nursing home in Wallington"},{"id":"B262-08","when":"No. 262","p":4,"h":"DAVE McMULLEN 1920-2007","note":"born 8 September 1920; joined 1 February 1940; died September 2007; race walker"},{"id":"B262-11","when":"No. 262","p":5,"h":"From The Belgravian – 50 Years Ago … 1958","note":"1958: second in Surrey 10 miles walk"}],"wrote":[{"id":"B182-69","when":"September 1973","p":41,"h":"PERCY WILSON"},{"id":"B183-16","when":"December 1973","p":7,"h":"THREE VET'S TO HAMBURG"}],"photos":[{"f":"crops/B227/B227-p29-kingsmeadow-1500-1997.jpg","c":"Above: Fortythree years later and the old codger's still on the move! 24th August 1997 and Chas. (174) lines up for the Veterans A.C. 1500 metres Championship at Kingsmeadow. His time was ... well we won't go into that ... but is this a good case for euthanasia? Maybe we should pay him not to wear our club kit! Seriously though, 1,500 metres is now way over his best distance because in 1998 Chas became the Surrey County M70 Champion over 100 metres!\n\nThird from the left, standing back, is Dave McMullen and wearing 62 is 5,000 metre ace from the '50s and current UK Athletics Council Member - Chris Chataway.","id":"B227-62","w":"March 1999"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B227/B227-p29-kingsmeadow-1500-1997.jpg","caption":"Above: Fortythree years later and the old codger's still on the move! 24th August 1997 and Chas. (174) lines up for the Veterans A.C. 1500 metres Championship at Kingsmeadow. His time was ... well we won't go into that ... but is this a good case for euthanasia? Maybe we should pay him not to wear our club kit! Seriously though, 1,500 metres is now way over his best distance because in 1998 Chas became the Surrey County M70 Champion over 100 metres!\n\nThird from the left, standing back, is Dave McMullen and wearing 62 is 5,000 metre ace from the '50s and current UK Athletics Council Member - Chris Chataway.","source":"B227-62","when":"March 1999"},"x":1,"share":{"d":"Dave McMullen in The Belgravian